---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={`About — ${SITE_TITLE}`} description="About MidMon — edge-AI condition monitoring for mid-market manufacturers." />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main class="pt-36 md:pt-44 pb-24">
			<section class="container-x">
				<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
					<span class="section-eyebrow">About</span>
					<h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight md:text-6xl">
						We&rsquo;re building MidMon for the <span class="text-gradient-accent">plants the incumbents ignore</span>.
					</h1>
					<p class="mt-6 text-lg text-[var(--color-text-muted)]">
						MidMon is an edge-AI condition monitoring platform built specifically for mid-market
						manufacturers &mdash; the 30,000+ plants in Canada and the US Northeast that operate
						between 50 and 500 critical assets but can&rsquo;t justify the seven-figure cost of an
						enterprise predictive maintenance deployment.
					</p>

					<div class="mt-12 space-y-6 text-[var(--color-text-muted)]">
						<p>
							We started MidMon at Concordia University&rsquo;s Gina Cody School of Engineering in
							2025. Six undergraduate engineers, each with a named leadership role in IEEE or
							CSME, each owning exactly one of the disciplines the platform depends on: FPGA
							architecture, RF signal processing, edge ML, embedded systems, cloud integration,
							and industrial B2B sales.
						</p>
						<p>
							The technical insight is simple: a purpose-built FPGA-NPU codesign can run
							transformer-class anomaly detection in real time on under 5 watts &mdash; making it
							possible, for the first time, to deliver enterprise-grade predictive maintenance
							at a price a plant manager can approve unilaterally.
						</p>
						<p>
							The product insight is simpler: the mid-market doesn&rsquo;t need a managed service.
							It needs a sensor it can bolt on in fifteen minutes that sends a plain-language
							alert when something is about to break.
						</p>
						<p>
							That&rsquo;s what we&rsquo;re building. If you run a plant, invest in industrial AI, or want to
							help us build it &mdash; <a class="text-white underline decoration-[#2dd4bf]/40 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-[#2dd4bf]" href="/#contact">we&rsquo;d love to hear from you</a>.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="mt-12 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
						<a href="/#how" class="btn btn-primary">See how it works</a>
						<a href="/#contact" class="btn btn-ghost">Talk to the team</a>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
